# Mapbox access token (optional).
# The map works out of the box with free OpenStreetMap tiles; set this to upgrade
# to Mapbox street/satellite tiles.
#
# Local:  copy this file to `.env` and paste your token below.
# Vercel: add VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN under Project Settings → Environment Variables,
#         enable it for the Production environment, then REDEPLOY. Vite inlines
#         VITE_-prefixed variables at build time, so an existing deployment keeps
#         whatever value it was built with.
#
# Must be a public token (pk.…) — secret tokens (sk.…) cannot be used in a
# browser. Paste the raw value, no surrounding quotes. If the token has URL
# restrictions, add your deployment origin or Mapbox will answer 403.
#
# Get a free token at https://account.mapbox.com
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq (GroqCloud) — powers the WhatsApp auto-reply.
#
# Free tier: get a key at https://console.groq.com (keys look like gsk_…).
# Without a key the demo answers with its built-in keyword bot, so this is
# optional. With one, each driver message is answered by Groq using that
# conversation's memory object (driver, vehicle, trip, alerts, remembered facts
# and recent transcript) as context.
#
# WARNING: VITE_ variables are inlined into the browser bundle, so a key set
# here is readable by anyone who opens the site. Use a throwaway free-tier key
# you can rotate.
# For anything real, leave this blank and set VITE_GROQ_PROXY_URL instead.
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=

# Model id. Defaults to llama-3.3-70b-versatile. Other free-tier options include
# llama-3.1-8b-instant (fastest) and openai/gpt-oss-20b.
VITE_GROQ_MODEL=

# Optional: an OpenAI-compatible endpoint that holds the key server-side.
# When set, requests go to {VITE_GROQ_PROXY_URL}/chat/completions with no key in
# the browser. Also the fix if the browser blocks api.groq.com on CORS.
VITE_GROQ_PROXY_URL=
